00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:01,210
Guest.

263
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:01,210
Fancy guest.

264
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:03,340
Two seconds.

265
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:03,340
Uh, 11?

266
00:14:04,710 --> 00:14:06,670
Eleven. Unbelievable. Eleven is correct.

267
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,470
Yes!

268
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,470
Ha-ha-ha.

269
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:11,590
"Chandler was how old when he first touched a girl's breast?"

270
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:13,050
Fourteen?

271
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:13,050
No, 19.

272
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,810
Thanks, man.

273
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:17,180
"Joey had an imaginary childhood friend.

274
00:14:17,350 --> 00:14:19,190
His name was?"

275
00:14:17,350 --> 00:14:19,190
Maurice.

276
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,230
"His profession was?"

277
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,230
Space cowboy!

278
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,810
Correct.

279
00:14:23,770 --> 00:14:26,030
"What is Chandler Bing's job?"

280
00:14:27,990 --> 00:14:29,030
Oh.

281
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:30,820
Oh, gosh.

282
00:14:30,990 --> 00:14:32,620
Ten seconds. You need this or you lose.

283
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,910
It has something to do with transponding.

284
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:38,660
Oh! Oh! He's a transponster.

285
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:40,870
That's not even a word!

286
00:14:41,710 --> 00:14:42,790
Oh, my God.

287
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,920
Oh, my God.

288
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,920
No!

289
00:14:49,170 --> 00:14:50,260
Whoo!

290
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:55,430
You know what? You are mean boys who are just being mean.

291
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:58,980
Hey, don't get mad at us. No one forced you to raise the stakes.

292
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:01,690
That is not true. She did. She forced me.

293
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:04,440
We'd still be here if you hadn't got the question wrong.

294
00:15:04,610 --> 00:15:06,940
Well, it was a stupid, unfair question!

295
00:15:07,110 --> 00:15:08,780
Don't blame the questions!

296
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:11,030
Would you all stop yelling in our apartment?

297
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:14,450
You are ruining moving day for us.

298
00:15:14,910 --> 00:15:16,200
Chandler!

299
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:22,210
Chandler, I saw what you were doing through the window.

300
00:15:22,370 --> 00:15:25,540
I saw what you were doing to my sister. Now, get out here!

301
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:28,880
Well, listen, we had a good run.

302
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:30,970
You know? What was it? Four, five months?

303
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:33,380
That's more than most people have in a lifetime.

304
00:15:33,550 --> 00:15:35,850
So goodbye, take care, bye-bye then.

305
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:39,020
Hey, Ross. What's up, bro?

306
00:15:41,270 --> 00:15:45,230
What the hell are you doing?

307
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,480
Hey, what's going on?

308
00:15:46,650 --> 00:15:50,740
Well, I think... I think Ross knows about me and Monica.

309
00:15:51,610 --> 00:15:54,280
Dude, he's right there.

310
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:59,240
I thought you were my best friend. This is my sister.

311
00:15:59,410 --> 00:16:02,580
My best friend and my sister. I cannot believe this.

312
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:06,580
We're not just messing around. I love her.

313
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:08,540
Okay? I'm in love with her.

314
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:12,970
I'm so sorry that you had to find out this way.

315
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:17,010
I'm sorry, but it's true. I love him too.

316
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:25,770
My best friend and my sister.

317
00:16:28,690 --> 00:16:31,070
I cannot believe this.

318
00:16:32,530 --> 00:16:34,320
This is the last box of your clothes.

319
00:16:34,490 --> 00:16:37,450
I'm just gonna label it "What were you thinking?"

320
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:42,500
Funny, I was just gonna go across the hall and write that on Chandler.

321
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:47,830
Okay, you guys, I don't mean to make things worse, but...

322
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,380
...I don't wanna live with Rachel anymore.

323
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:53,130
What?

324
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:53,130
You're just so mean to each other.

325
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:56,550
And I don't wanna end up like that with Rachel. I still like you.

326
00:16:57,050 --> 00:16:59,430
Well, Phoebe, that's fine because I'm not moving.

327
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,720
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Phoebe, you gotta take her.

328
00:17:03,810 --> 00:17:05,520
I know I said some bad stuff...

329
00:17:05,690 --> 00:17:08,860
...but Rachel does have some qualities that make her a good roommate.

330
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:10,480
She gets tons of catalogs...

331
00:17:10,650 --> 00:17:14,190
...and, um, she'll fold down the pages of the things she thinks I'd like.

332
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:16,950
What else?

333
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:16,950
Uh...

334
00:17:17,110 --> 00:17:19,370
When I take a shower...

335
00:17:19,530 --> 00:17:21,660
...she leaves me little notes on the mirror.

336
00:17:21,870 --> 00:17:24,080
Yeah, I do. I do do that.

337
00:17:24,250 --> 00:17:28,290
That's nice. I like having things to read in the bathroom.

338
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:33,000
When I fall asleep on the couch after reading...

339
00:17:34,130 --> 00:17:36,220
...she covers me over with a blanket.

340
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:40,340
Well, you know, I don't want you to be cold.

341
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:47,100
And when I told her I was gonna move in with Chandler...

342
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:49,480
...she was really supportive.

343
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:53,940
[SOBBING] You were so great.

344
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,990
You made it so easy.

345
00:17:59,450 --> 00:18:02,030
And now you have to leave.

346
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,700
And I have to live with a boy!

347
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,550
Hey.

348
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:24,680
She really left.

349
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:24,680
I know.

350
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:30,440
Thank you.

351
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:30,440
No problem, roomie.

352
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:40,400
Can I ask you a question?

353
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:40,400
Sure.

354
00:18:40,570 --> 00:18:43,280
What the hell is that dog doing here?

355
00:18:44,410 --> 00:18:46,830
A little toast here. Ding, ding, ding.

356
00:18:44,410 --> 00:18:46,830
Mm.

357
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,040
This isn't exactly the kind of Thanksgiving you planned...

358
00:18:50,210 --> 00:18:53,920
...but for me this has been really great, you know?

359
00:18:54,090 --> 00:18:57,550
I think because it didn't involve divorce...

360
00:18:57,710 --> 00:18:59,010
...or projectile vomiting.

361
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:03,930
I was just thinking, if you'd gone to Vail...

362
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:07,930
...or if you guys had been with your family, or if you didn't have...

363
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:09,770
...syphilis and stuff...

364
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:13,980
...we wouldn't be all together, you know?

365
00:19:14,150 --> 00:19:15,900
So I guess what I'm trying to say...

366
00:19:16,070 --> 00:19:21,990
...is that I'm very thankful that all of your Thanksgivings sucked.

367
00:19:22,990 --> 00:19:24,660
That's so sweet.

368
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:26,490
Thank you.

369
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:27,700
Mm.

370
00:19:28,450 --> 00:19:30,750
And hey, here's to a lousy Christmas.

371
00:19:30,910 --> 00:19:32,170
And a crappy New Year.

372
00:19:32,330 --> 00:19:34,790
Hear, hear.

373
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:42,970
You can't move. You just... You just can't.

374
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:45,800
Rachel's right. This is where you guys belong.

375
00:19:45,970 --> 00:19:49,520
You don't wanna live in Westchester. That's the worst of the Chesters.

376
00:19:50,810 --> 00:19:54,310
You know, sometimes when I'm alone in my apartment, I look over here...

377
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:57,820
...and you guys are just having dinner...

378
00:19:57,980 --> 00:20:00,900
...or watching TV or something...

379
00:20:01,570 --> 00:20:03,280
...but it makes me feel better.

380
00:20:03,450 --> 00:20:05,950
And now when I look over, who am I gonna see?

381
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:09,120
The Gottliebs? The Yangs?

382
00:20:09,490 --> 00:20:11,370
They don't make me feel so good.

383
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:16,880
Yeah. So don't move, okay? Just stay here...

384
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:19,300
...and maybe close your blinds at night.

385
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:19,300
Hey.

386
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,470
Hello?

387
00:20:30,310 --> 00:20:32,350
It's Nancy. They responded to our offer.

388
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:33,810
And?

389
00:20:34,850 --> 00:20:36,440
Yeah...

390
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,900
Okay. Thanks.

391
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:41,940
They passed.

392
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:46,450
They said they won't go a penny under the asking price.

393
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:49,490
We can't afford that.

394
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:49,490
I know.

395
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:53,120
Well, there you go.

396
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,630
I'm really sorry, you guys.

397
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:04,010
Yeah, I'm sorry too. I'm even more sorry that phone call didn't come...

398
00:21:04,170 --> 00:21:07,050
...before I told you about looking through the window.

399
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:09,600
Yeah. Well, we're gonna let you be alone.

400
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:11,720
You gonna be okay?

401
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:11,720
Yeah, we'll be okay.

402
00:21:11,890 --> 00:21:13,930
Love you guys.

403
00:21:15,770 --> 00:21:18,600
You know, I'm really sorry I wasn't more supportive before.

404
00:21:18,810 --> 00:21:20,360
That's okay. We understand.

405
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:22,360
Yeah, and about this Nancy...

406
00:21:22,530 --> 00:21:24,610
If you're not sleeping with her, should I?

407
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:34,250
I know there'll be other houses, but I just, uh...

408
00:21:34,410 --> 00:21:37,580
I loved that one so much.

409
00:21:34,410 --> 00:21:37,580
Yeah.

410
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:40,130
Well, it's a good thing we got it then.

411
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:43,840
What?

412
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:43,840
We got the house.

413
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:47,590
Oh, my God.

414
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:47,590
I didn't wanna tell you in front of them.

415
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:49,340
We got it? We got the house?

416
00:21:49,510 --> 00:21:51,470
We're getting a house.

417
00:21:49,510 --> 00:21:51,470
Oh!

418
00:21:53,890 --> 00:21:54,930
Mm.

419
00:21:55,430 --> 00:21:58,190
We're getting a house.

420
00:21:55,430 --> 00:21:58,190
And a baby.

421
00:21:58,350 --> 00:21:59,770
We're growing up.

422
00:22:01,230 --> 00:22:02,650
We sure are.

423
00:22:03,610 --> 00:22:04,690
Who's gonna tell them?

424
00:22:04,860 --> 00:22:07,110
Not it.

425
00:22:04,860 --> 00:22:07,110
Not it. Damn it!

426
00:22:11,870 --> 00:22:13,530
And, Rachel, this is yours.

427
00:22:11,870 --> 00:22:13,530
Aah!

428
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:15,410
Why? What are these for?

429
00:22:15,580 --> 00:22:18,330
You'll see.

430
00:22:15,580 --> 00:22:18,330
All right, everybody open them.

431
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:23,040
Oh, wow, this is so beautiful.

432
00:22:23,210 --> 00:22:26,050
Oh, these are the ones I was looking at in the store.

433
00:22:26,210 --> 00:22:28,130
I know.

434
00:22:26,210 --> 00:22:28,130
Oh, I love this.

435
00:22:28,300 --> 00:22:30,720
A meatball sub.

436
00:22:30,930 --> 00:22:32,260
Thanks.

437
00:22:32,430 --> 00:22:35,060
Seriously, guys, what's going on? What are these for?

438
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:38,390
Well, I didn't know how to tell you before...

439
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,520
...but we got the house.

440
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,520
Enjoy.

441
00:22:45,730 --> 00:22:46,820
What did they say?

